1
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:30,320
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

2
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:35,560
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

3
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:38,320
♪ I don't understand ♪

4
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:43,720
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

5
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:48,920
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

6
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:55,080
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

7
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:00,680
Since Parn started seeing you,
she hasn't been working here anymore.

8
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:02,320
But she's still accepting clients.

9
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:04,200
Sis Mol owed ten million to a loan shark.

10
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,480
She came to help,
so they wouldn't take over this place.

11
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:09,200
If you love Peem, let her go.

12
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,520
Didn't she tell you that I'm gay?

13
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,440
You misunderstood Parn.

14
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,800
Get yourself together before it's too late

15
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,240
to win her back.

16
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:20,800
Opening day.

17
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,280
Hey.

18
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,440
Do you think I should tell her?

19
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,320
I don't think you should.

20
00:01:34,759 --> 00:01:36,160
It's good that she's moved on.

21
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,800
Plus, today is a good day.

22
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,200
If you bring that up, it'll ruin the mood.

23
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,479
You're right.

24
00:01:44,039 --> 00:01:45,120
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

25
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:49,640
How long have you been here?

26
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,600
- Parn!
- Miew! Pat!

27
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,120
Sis isn't coming. She can't.

28
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,240
It's okay. So that's why I haven't seen her.

29
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,880
Someone is courting her.

30
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,280
He's rich too.

31
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:04,800
Who is it?

32
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:06,880
It's Tot.

33
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:08,639
Huh? Really?

34
00:02:08,919 --> 00:02:09,880
- Yes.
- Yes.

35
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:15,160
- Alright, let's give her our well wishes.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

36
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,400
But let me go first.

37
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,560
Sure.

38
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,440
Here you go!

39
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:27,280
Ahem! I wish for your shop
to become a massive success!

40
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:30,120
Let your success ring around the world!

41
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,000
I hope you make a big profit.

42
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,640
Whatever you're selling,
I hope it sells like it's free.

43
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,079
May you get so rich,

44
00:02:40,079 --> 00:02:43,560
you'll beg for it to stop!

45
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,040
Ridiculously rich!

46
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,320
Sadhu!

47
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,040
Here.

48
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,600
It's lucky money.

49
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,640
Yeah, take it.

50
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,079
Thank you.

51
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:10,120
I knew it! My gaydar was beeping so hard.

52
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,240
Techin also left me the bakery's business card.

53
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,400
Oh my.

54
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,640
What a nice guy.

55
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:20,560
Did he leave his card for me too?

56
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:25,000
So no.

57
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,440
Fine, keep going.

58
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,640
Parn only accepts jobs that involve serving drinks
and drinking with clients,

59
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:31,680
but she won't sleep with them.

60
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,640
As for meal dates, she only goes
with those she already knows and trusts.

61
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,840
Mm.

62
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:40,760
That means Parn had never slept with her clients.

63
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,079
She said I was the first.

64
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:47,280
Well, I guess it's true.

65
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,800
How will she ever repay five million to me?

66
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,720
How long will running a bakery take
to pay off the debt?

67
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,960
And now you're worried about her?

68
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,920
Turns out you've misunderstood her
all this time, about everything.

69
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,360
Yeah.

70
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,960
What are you going to do next?

71
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:08,960
Ugh!

72
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:11,560
I really thought she was deceiving me.

73
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,560
Stop it.

74
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,880
Stop trying to justify your thoughts.

75
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:19,519
Right now, you need to figure out
what you're going to do.

76
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:22,760
So?

77
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,320
You love her.

78
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:32,520
Yeah.

79
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,840
And very much too.

80
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,320
I do.

81
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,760
Go make up with her then.

82
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,000
- I do want to.
- Oh?

83
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,000
- Hey!
- Don't "hey" me.

84
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,800
Go make up with her if you want to.
Why stay stubborn?

85
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,800
If you love her,
there's no need for any reasons.

86
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,080
Go patch things up with her. Just go.

87
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,760
It's not that simple.

88
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,520
I put her through quite a lot.

89
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,920
If you put her through a lot,

90
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:03,480
put just as much effort into winning her back.

91
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,760
But she put me through a lot too.

92
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,520
Why did she have to lie to me?

93
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,640
If she'd told me, I'd have been happy to help.

94
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:13,160
Then just forget it.

95
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,200
Let her go.

96
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,840
That way, you can also meet someone new.

97
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,640
Whatever you gave her,
just think of it as a gesture of affection.

98
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,640
It won't put a dent in your bank account, right?

99
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,640
More importantly,

100
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:28,360
hatred is never appeased by hatred.

101
00:05:30,080 --> 00:05:34,320
Whatever wrong she's done to you,
let karma take its course.

102
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,480
And why do I have to let her go so easily?

103
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,000
She hurt me.
Does she think she can live a good life now?

104
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,520
Since karma isn't fast enough,

105
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:45,840
Parn will have to face me.

106
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:47,960
Huh?

107
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:58,320
Whoa!

108
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:00,880
Parn!

109
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:02,680
Please come in.

110
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:05,240
Please come in.

111
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,800
Pan Pas...

112
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,120
Pan Pastry-ne!

113
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,040
What's with the name?

114
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,360
Parn and Phakanee?

115
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,360
Yeah.

116
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:34,840
You used her money to open a shop,
so you named it after her?

117
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:36,680
Are you crazy?

118
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,120
Hey!

119
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,240
- First order!
- First order!

120
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:56,200
Hey, wait. Ding, ding, ding...

121
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,200
Whoa!

122
00:06:58,960 --> 00:06:59,960
Is the machine broken?

123
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,960
The orders keep coming in.

124
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:02,960
Isn't it good?

125
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,760
Oh...

126
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,240
Let's close the shop.

127
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:16,240
Yeah, before my body shuts down.

128
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,720
Hey.

129
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:27,360
If I'd known a bakery would sell this well,

130
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,880
I wouldn't be working at the club.

131
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,240
Come on, Miew.

132
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:36,080
That means they must taste good.

133
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,520
You can't even fry an egg without burning it.

134
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:39,800
And you think you can bake?

135
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,240
Pat! Ugh!

136
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,120
Come on, you two.

137
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:48,080
- Jeez!
- Jeez, you still haven't turned it off?

138
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:50,720
Oh, no.

139
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:55,159
I can't go on. My hands are shaking.

140
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,080
I'll give you a massage.

141
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:05,560
Seriously? She's still accepting orders?

142
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:09,400
There's nothing here.

143
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,920
Huh?

144
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,120
Oh, right.

145
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:18,520
It's my phone. Sis texted me.

146
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,200
- Ugh!
- Ugh!

147
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:21,560
Sorry.

148
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:25,920
If one more order comes in,
I'll drop dead here.

149
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,840
When the delivery driver gets here,
just let them take me instead.

150
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,440
Straight to the temple.

151
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,520
- Kusala Dhamma...
- Quit it.

152
00:08:34,799 --> 00:08:36,039
It's a good day today.

153
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,440
- I forgot.
- I can't believe you two.

154
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,840
It's true that you got a lot of orders,

155
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:44,240
but when I was sorting them,
I only saw one name.

156
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,320
- Really?
- Yeah.

157
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,360
Won't they get diabetes at this rate?

158
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:50,760
Right.

159
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:53,600
I was so busy getting the orders ready
I didn't notice.

160
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,000
Do you remember the name?

161
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,680
I think it's Pee...

162
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,920
Pee...

163
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,680
Peekinak.

164
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,440
Peekinak?

165
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,760
Mm.

166
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:16,880
She must have died right at the oven.

167
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,120
Ms. Peem.

168
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,480
What should we do with these?

169
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:26,080
Bring me a box to try.
I doubt it'll be any good.

170
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:28,800
Give the rest away to the staff and my friends.

171
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,680
The last one.

172
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,960
It's so good.

173
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,920
The cake isn't too sweet,
and it's so smooth. Perfect!

174
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,360
It's so good!

175
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,960
I'll tire you out even more tomorrow.

176
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,360
Okay...

177
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,480
So she can still handle it.

178
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:16,320
She got good reviews too.

179
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,080
"The pastries are delicious."

180
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,240
"The owner is pretty."

181
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,280
You drove 30 kilometers for this?

182
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:37,000
Who forced you?
Why didn't you buy something nearby?

183
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,920
"Just seeing the owner is refreshing."

184
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,320
Oh, please. It's a cake shop.

185
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:07,800
Ow!

186
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,720
Why don't you get up?

187
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,560
Why are you sitting there?

188
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:30,280
Why didn't you tell me Techin is gay?

189
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:40,880
Why didn't you answer me?

190
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:41,960
Didn't you hear me?

191
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:50,000
I heard you, but I didn't want to answer.

192
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:54,400
Will it kill you to answer?

193
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:00,240
You like him because he's rich, don't you?

194
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,120
But I'm richer, you know?

195
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,360
Plus, he likes guys, not girls like you.

196
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,160
What? You want to fix a gay man?

197
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:09,440
Is that even possible?

198
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,240
He's gay. It's not like he has a cold.

199
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,680
Just like me. I love you.

200
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,240
Even if there were 100 other men,
I'd still love you.

201
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,320
It can't be fixed.

202
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:25,560
Ms. Peem!

203
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:29,040
You have no right to do that to me.

204
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,440
Why?

205
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,160
So I can't do it unless I pay?

206
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:43,080
Will you stop saying things
to hurt my feelings like this?

207
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,280
I thought you didn't want to see my face.

208
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,800
Why are you here?

209
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,600
I'm here to buy these buildings.

210
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:54,440
Then go look at them.

211
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,320
Just leave me alone.

212
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,600
Hey.

213
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:22,080
You called me here just to ignore me?

214
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:24,240
Am I supposed to talk to the table?

215
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,440
Parn said things between us were over.

216
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,840
Well, you broke up with her.

217
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:35,920
I did.

218
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,920
But it's not my fault, is it?

219
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:40,280
She broke her promise, so I broke up with her.

220
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:43,200
She had a date with Techin
and a job at Paradise.

221
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:46,720
But now you know
they're not what you thought they were.

222
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,680
So what?

223
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:52,160
I told you to patch things up,
but you ended up getting slapped.

224
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,000
I tried to.

225
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:58,040
By ordering her pastries for the entire country?

226
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,080
No.

227
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,960
Then why did you do that?

228
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:06,800
I just wanted to work her so hard
she'd collapse right there by the oven.

229
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,760
Really?

230
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:09,880
Yeah.

231
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:14,800
Or were you just helping her business grow?

232
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:21,480
You're such a Siberian Husky.

233
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:22,920
What do you mean?

234
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,320
You're stubborn, self-centered,
and bark at everything.

235
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,880
You're exaggerating.

236
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,760
Yet you do love her.

237
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,840
Instead of patching things up, you insulted her.

238
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,800
Then you kissed her and got slapped for it.

239
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,760
How are you ever going
to get back together with her?

240
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
It's for Ms. Parn.

241
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,400
(Parn - From Peem)

242
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,080
Wait.

243
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:03,640
Yes?

244
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,720
Please return it.

245
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:10,960
Return?

246
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,400
Why did she return it?

247
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:17,600
Excuse me, Ms. Peem.

248
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:24,240
I was trying to make up with you.

249
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,200
Thank you.

250
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,160
Why didn't you accept the flowers?

251
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,920
You have the right to send them.
I have the right to refuse them.

252
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:56,800
What's wrong with you?

253
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,080
I should be asking you.

254
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:01,520
You said you didn't want to see me,
but you keep coming.

255
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,160
If you're open,
you have to serve your customers.

256
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,280
I'm a customer, aren't I?

257
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:07,160
We're closed now.
We're not accepting any more customers.

258
00:17:09,079 --> 00:17:10,560
You're not accepting customers
who come for the cakes.

259
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,960
But do you still accept customers
who want a meal date?

260
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,560
Or just those looking for intimacy?

261
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:19,319
Ms. Peem!

262
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,440
Stop doing this to me.

263
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:25,839
I'm a human being too.

264
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,240
Get out.

265
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,760
I said get out!

266
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:47,240
Oh my. Serves you right.

267
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,320
I didn't call you here to rub it in.

268
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,640
You brought it upon yourself.

269
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,680
That wasn't patching things up.
You were just being an asshole.

270
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,640
I've never had to win anyone back before.

271
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:04,600
I just got angry when she stood up to me.

272
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,480
I'm sorry.

273
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,880
Why did you apologize to me?

274
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,640
Try saying it.

275
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,560
Say what?

276
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:16,840
Say you're sorry.

277
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,160
"I'm sorry."

278
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,480
Are you insane?

279
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,920
Why should I apologize to you?

280
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,880
It's a practice. So you can say it to Parn.

281
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:28,800
But I guess someone like you
doesn't know how to say it.

282
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:35,160
I'm sorry for making you feel bad that night.

283
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,240
I've said it before.

284
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,200
I know how to do it.

285
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,280
Then say it to her.

286
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:50,800
If money can't win her forgiveness, try this.

287
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,800
Feelings can't be bought with money.

288
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,760
They come from the heart.

289
00:18:57,920 --> 00:19:01,680
Gosh. Earlier, you just said,
"Parn will have to face me."

290
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:02,680
How did that go, huh?

291
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:09,640
Why do you look so dejected?

292
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,560
I've never seen you like this before.

293
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:17,560
Be confident.

294
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:21,760
Just like when you insulted her, yeah?

295
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,400
Hey, are you mocking me?

296
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:25,640
No.

297
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,080
Just offering some advice.

298
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:29,520
You should be confident.

299
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:33,160
After all, your father is a business tycoon.

300
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:36,080
And you're a third-generation heir
to the Traisuvetthiwat family,

301
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:40,920
which owns the biggest shopping mall in Thailand.

302
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:49,120
Hey.

303
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:02,240
Parn, didn't you hear me?

304
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:07,240
Huh? What is it?

305
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:10,040
Jeez.

306
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,960
She's been calling you for a while now.

307
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:12,880
Really?

308
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,040
- Yes.
- Yes.

309
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,600
What's wrong?

310
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,160
Must be about Ms. Peem, huh?

311
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:21,600
Come on, tell us.

312
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,480
Who summoned the Devil?

313
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:34,960
No one did.

314
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,040
Let's go.

315
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:43,760
Well, we'll go out to grab a bite.

316
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:44,920
We'll buy something for you too.

317
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,480
Please make yourself comfortable.

318
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,720
You can sit over there.

319
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,280
You don't love me anymore?

320
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,840
I shouldn't love you.

321
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,680
Why not?

322
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:30,400
You said you didn't want to see my face.

323
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,440
How do you know that?

324
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:34,280
You told me to get out of your life.

325
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,480
I want to come see you every day.

326
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:46,000
You drove me away like I was some kind of animal.

327
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:50,360
What are you trying to get out of this?

328
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:58,680
Am I just some toy you rich people can play with?

329
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:01,800
You buy me when you want me,

330
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,400
toss me aside when you're bored,

331
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,360
then come back
whenever you feel like playing with me again.

332
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,480
I've never seen you as a plaything.

333
00:22:14,360 --> 00:22:15,880
Then what do you see me as?

334
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,360
You're the person I love.

335
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:34,880
I'm sorry.

336
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,320
Please don't do this.

337
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,680
I don't want to go back to where I was.

338
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,560
Where you were?

339
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:12,800
What do you mean by that?

340
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,280
A place where people view me as a worthless woman.

341
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,280
You and your family will never forget my past.

342
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:23,680
It doesn't matter what other people think.

343
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,120
Even though you've quit,

344
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:29,640
the people who knew you or have met you...

345
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:33,320
will still remember your past.

346
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:35,120
Even if Peem doesn't care,

347
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,400
people in her social circle...

348
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:40,640
won't stop talking about it.

349
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:43,880
If you love Peem, let her go.

350
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:51,880
Please leave.

351
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,240
And don't come back again.

352
00:23:58,920 --> 00:23:59,920
Parn.

353
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:02,920
Why are you doing this?

354
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:04,560
Huh?

355
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:13,080
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

356
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:18,280
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

357
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:20,480
♪ I don't understand ♪

358
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:21,800
Because I don't love you anymore.

359
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:26,520
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

360
00:24:26,520 --> 00:24:28,600
♪ Why won't they say... ♪

361
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:29,520
Parn...

362
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:31,680
♪ The same thing? ♪

363
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:38,440
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

364
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:46,160
♪ Just the one word, love ♪

365
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:51,720
♪ I don't understand why I can't say it ♪

366
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:55,560
♪ Why do I keep it to myself? ♪

367
00:24:55,560 --> 00:25:02,440
♪ I can only be angry with myself
For acting so cold ♪

368
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:07,680
♪ Making something so simple so complicated ♪

369
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:14,800
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

370
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:19,920
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

371
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:22,760
♪ I don't understand ♪

372
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:27,480
♪ What's wrong with my mouth and my heart? ♪

373
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,440
Parn.

374
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:33,440
♪ Why won't they say the same thing? ♪

375
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:40,440
♪ Will we ever get to love each other? ♪

376
00:25:55,720 --> 00:26:02,520
♪ Even though my heart says I love you ♪

377
00:26:02,840 --> 00:26:07,680
♪ Why am I like this? ♪

378
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:09,760
♪ I don't understand ♪

379
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:12,480
Our friend's definitely going to marry
a billionaire!

380
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:15,320
We don't have to eat street-side sausages anymore?

381
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,720
Forget grilled chicken.
Say hello to fancy steaks.

382
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:22,240
Ms. Peem?

383
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:25,640
What's going on?

384
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,000
I wonder that too.

385
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,760
Hey, are you alright?

386
00:26:32,840 --> 00:26:34,280
Are you okay?

387
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:49,200
I'm okay.

388
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:59,360
I think we can forget
about Parn marrying a billionaire.

389
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:02,440
You're right.

390
00:27:14,120 --> 00:27:15,040
Parn?

391
00:27:16,360 --> 00:27:17,520
Ms. Peem was crying.

392
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:18,840
And you're crying too?

393
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:20,000
What happened?

394
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:41,960
Can you tell us now, huh?

395
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,480
What did she do to you?

396
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:44,520
What did she say?

397
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:48,480
She told me she loved me.

398
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:51,520
Huh?

399
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:54,280
Then why did you two cry?

400
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:57,000
Happy tears?

401
00:28:00,760 --> 00:28:02,000
I chased her away.

402
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,400
What?

403
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:04,920
Why did you do that?

404
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,440
Why did you tell her to leave?

405
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:08,240
Why play hard to get?

406
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:11,520
I'm not playing hard to get.

407
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,360
Come on.

408
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:17,440
Just say it. Tell us everything.

409
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:22,480
It's not possible anyway.

410
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,400
She and I...

411
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:30,320
are too different.

412
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:37,400
It's okay...

413
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:47,480
It's so good.

414
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:49,360
I got to try it when Peem sent it to me.

415
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:50,680
That's why I came here.

416
00:28:51,240 --> 00:28:52,400
I'm not disappointed.

417
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:53,680
Thank you so much.

418
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:57,800
Thank you.

419
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:00,200
Hey.

420
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:03,160
Has Ms. Peem ever ordered from us?

421
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:04,480
Huh?

422
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,400
I've never seen her name.

423
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:09,160
Right. Doesn't ring the bell at all.

424
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:10,800
There's no Phakanee.

425
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:15,200
I'm sure there's none.

426
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,040
Oh, Pong?

427
00:29:23,280 --> 00:29:24,240
Parn.

428
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:26,560
How are you? Are you selling well?

429
00:29:26,560 --> 00:29:28,400
It's going well. We're sold out every day.

430
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:31,360
I brought my boss along too.

431
00:29:36,600 --> 00:29:37,680
Hello.

432
00:29:40,120 --> 00:29:42,240
Is she your sister, Pokpong?

433
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:44,320
Yes.

434
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:52,040
Alright, we'll go sit down.

435
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:03,880
The guy who's with your brother
has been to Paradise.

436
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:04,920
Really?

437
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:05,800
Yeah.

438
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:30,160
Will she let us in?

439
00:30:35,240 --> 00:30:36,080
Why are you here?

440
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:37,680
To talk to you.

441
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:41,440
Can we come in?

442
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:47,040
Whoa!

443
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:50,440
I can see the whole Bangkok from this room.

444
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,640
It's huge!

445
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:53,960
Miew, come here!

446
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:56,200
Girl!

447
00:30:56,520 --> 00:30:58,960
Have you taken your shoes off?
Her room is super clean.

448
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:03,360
Oh.

449
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:06,000
Uh, well, Ms.

450
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:09,400
Do you have any other friends
who have a place this big?

451
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:11,160
What? Ow!

452
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:13,800
What are you saying? Stop it!

453
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,800
We're here to talk about Parn.

454
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:27,080
What about her?

455
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:31,080
Parn loves you very much, Ms. Peem.

456
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:33,760
So what?

457
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:36,000
She told me not to go back to the shop.

458
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:41,680
- You say it. We've agreed.
- You say it!

459
00:31:43,280 --> 00:31:44,080
- You.
- You.

460
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:44,840
- You say it.
- You say it.

461
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,520
- You say it.
- Say it!

462
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,200
Your father won't let Parn date you!

463
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:53,400
He came to the shop
and offered Parn money to stop seeing you.

464
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:54,920
She agreed to stop seeing you,

465
00:31:55,280 --> 00:31:56,560
but she refused the money.

466
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:00,760
Is it true?

467
00:32:00,760 --> 00:32:01,760
Yes.

468
00:32:04,960 --> 00:32:07,720
We came here to beg you...

469
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:10,080
not to break up with Parn.

470
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:11,400
She really loves you.

471
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:17,840
What do I do to make her come around?

472
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:20,600
Just be yourself and she'll come around.

473
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:25,040
That's right. Just be yourself, Ms. Peem.
She'll come around.

474
00:32:32,560 --> 00:32:34,640
Pat, do you think it will work?

475
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:37,400
Of course. They love each other.

476
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:38,600
Really?

477
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:41,440
Maybe tonight, they might even

478
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:44,040
work, work, work it out together.

479
00:32:44,320 --> 00:32:47,560
You're right. They should keep making it work.

480
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:49,880
- Work, work, work.
- Work, work, work.

481
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,280
Let's go.

482
00:32:52,280 --> 00:32:53,680
Work, work, work.

483
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:56,040
(Thank you, everyone.
Today, we have zero food waste again.)

484
00:32:56,040 --> 00:32:58,960
(I was planning to have some drinking yogurt
to boost my energy but ran out of it.)

485
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:00,560
(Please don't forget to come again tomorrow.)

486
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:08,600
I know what kind of work your sister used to do.

487
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:12,960
She has quit.

488
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:14,960
She doesn't work there anymore.

489
00:33:15,880 --> 00:33:16,960
Is that so?

490
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:19,040
Yes.

491
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:21,440
So she doesn't drink with clients anymore?

492
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:22,960
No, she doesn't.

493
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:28,800
Then, can I ask you for a favor?

494
00:33:32,520 --> 00:33:33,760
I like your sister.

495
00:33:36,640 --> 00:33:38,680
Get her to meet with me,

496
00:33:39,760 --> 00:33:42,480
and I'll make sure your job
and salary are secure.

497
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:44,240
Deal?

498
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,760
Uh, I don't think I can do that.

499
00:33:58,760 --> 00:34:01,160
Parn, we have to go now.

500
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:04,280
Thank you for coming.

501
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Sure.

502
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:08,800
It's late. We should go.

503
00:34:09,679 --> 00:34:10,760
Parn can go home too.

504
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:25,800
So you have no ambition to move up?

505
00:34:28,639 --> 00:34:30,600
My sister has been through enough.

506
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,639
She's doing this...

507
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:36,480
because she doesn't want to go back to that job.

508
00:34:38,320 --> 00:34:41,560
And I respect her decision.

509
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:46,520
Huh.

510
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,679
There's no way she can quit.

511
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:09,960
It's so good.

512
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:11,760
I got to try it when Peem sent it to me.

513
00:35:11,760 --> 00:35:13,040
That's why I came here.

514
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:17,200
If it's true,

515
00:35:18,520 --> 00:35:20,200
her name should be on the bill.

516
00:35:28,760 --> 00:35:31,280
(Customer's name: Peekinak)

517
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:33,800
This person ordered a lot.

518
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:43,040
They bought everything on the first day.

519
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:44,960
(Customer's name: Peekinak)

520
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:48,760
Peekinak?

521
00:35:58,560 --> 00:36:00,240
I didn't order anything.

522
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:01,760
It's been paid.

523
00:36:10,840 --> 00:36:11,880
"Peekinak."

524
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:24,280
A delivery's here. It's already paid for.

525
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:25,880
Thank you.

526
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,000
Thank you.

527
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,720
Peekinak again?

528
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:39,280
Peekinak....

529
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:43,680
Phakanee?

530
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:48,880
Did Ms. Peem send these?

531
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:10,960
Ms. Peem.

532
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:21,520
I told you not to come see me again.

533
00:37:22,120 --> 00:37:23,520
Why don't you want to see me?

534
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,120
You don't love me anymore?

535
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:32,200
Just leave.

536
00:37:32,840 --> 00:37:34,400
Tell me you don't love me anymore.

537
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:38,440
If you can say it, I'll leave.

538
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:46,360
You're doing this because of my dad, right?

539
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:48,560
How do you know that?

540
00:37:48,560 --> 00:37:49,760
Shouldn't I know?

541
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:52,400
Pat and Mamiew told you, right?

542
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:54,920
Doesn't matter who told me.

543
00:37:56,800 --> 00:37:58,920
What matters is whether you still love me.

544
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:02,400
Even if I love you,

545
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:04,520
it's not possible.

546
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:13,120
Why do you think it's impossible?

547
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:21,640
Our statuses are not equal.

548
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:23,960
So what?

549
00:38:27,520 --> 00:38:29,120
If you're with me,

550
